Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 11/18/2024]
1. Er = 1567 keV: since the 2+_2 level in 32Ar has not been observed yet, the resonance energy is calculated from the Coulomb shift estimate of Herndl et al. 1995.
   We adopt an uncertainty of 150 keV; note that the first excited state energy is only reproduced by the Coulomb shift calculations within 60 keV. The proton 
   partial width is estimated using the shell model; for the gamma-ray partial width, the geometric mean of the shell-model value and that calculated from the 
   experimental lifetime of the 32Si mirror level is adopted. 
2. The direct capture S factor is estimated using the shell-model spectroscopic factors of Herndl et al. 1995.
